A||N||3||chester||Adjustable back pressure.||||5||
Z||000000||chester||07-05-2001||08:52 AM||||Hi all,<P>I am looking for a means of adjusting my back pressure.  I know that I can use supertrapps but I would like to keep the exhaust look stock.  I currently have a 2.8 with headers that dump into a 2 1/4" pipe.  For now I have the stock exhaust plumbed to it with no cat.  The motor is heavily modified and breaths well. One thing I have noticed is that my power band is higher then I was anticipating.  Low end torque is ok but I would like more.  Highway HP is way too much.  I know back pressure is minimal now and with a complete 2 1/4" exhaust and the flowmaster I have, I know it will drop it even more so I want a means of tuning it.  Does anyone know of a back pressure adjustment device that is inline to the exhaust?  If all else fails does anyone know of a reason why I couldn't use the disk only supertrapp ends with the flowmaster to give me tuning ability? Has anyone addressed this in their performance setup? I really don't want to go that route but will if I have no choice. Thanks in advance!<P>Rob D.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tom88gt||07-05-2001||09:35 AM||||JC Whitney has some kinda automatically adjustable "back pressure" exhaust tips.  Never seen them before.  They have the usual JCW wild performance claims.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Will||07-05-2001||10:14 AM||||If you really want to get wild and crazy, you could put a servo or solenoid operated butterfly valve inline in your exhaust. It would normally be half closed to allow exhaust flow but increase back pressure. Some simple electronic controls would open it all the way when you rev the engine past a certain RPM.<BR>Ferrari does this on the 360 to have a dual length exhaust system, one length tuned for low RPM, one for high.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||07-05-2001||03:07 PM||||If you really want to increase your bottom end you could advance you camshaft timing 3 degrees. If you give me your camshaft specifications I can show you what you could expect from doing this. <P>By the way I was cruising through the archives and saw a picture of your car. Looks really mean! I like it. Can’t wait to see your car at the track. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
